Track 1: Pier 44 Smuggled Your Return Slip
- Story & Context: Producer J-Slip cut this track after finding an undelivered parcel crushed beneath an automated straddle carrier on Berth 3, its waterproof ink smeared across a manifest dated three winters back. He recorded the dry, hydraulic snap of the dock's perimeter gates slamming shut to layer under the 808 clap, contrasting the violent mechanical percussion with featherlight Rhodes keys. As the harbor's navigation beacons groaned their low G-sharp warnings through the haze, Miri stepped up to a moisture-logged condenser mic and sang, "Left my tracking number in your cold grease, but you sailed before the customs cleared the dock."
