Track 2: S.O.S. Stamp (Postage Due)
- Story & Context: Conceived during a thirty-six-hour port lockdown when uncrewed cargo ships stacked up outside the channel, blowing mournful horn signals that rattled the tin walls of the duo’s squat. The rhythm relies on a syncopated, whip-cracking handclap that stutters like an errant telegraph key against a sluggish pluggnb bass slide. Miri wrote the track as an open letter to an offshore cable inspector who drifted out of range, whispering into her autotune unit, "Wrote you thirty pages on the shipping log, but the envelope arrived without a seal."
