Track 3: Did You Hear the Hull Call Back?
- Story & Context: Local folklore claims this track preserves the final unauthorized radio exchange between the lost container vessel Ameland and the shore radar before the ship was scuttled by harbor drones. J-Slip layered two opposing low-frequency synth horns eight bars apart—one in the far-left ear, one in the far-right—letting them decay into an enormous, reverberant double-clap that sounds like steel plating buckling under ocean depth. Over the cavernous, drifting ambient coda, Miri delivers the scene's most famous hook: "I threw two flares up into the grey, but you answered with an engine blast and turned away."
